<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # My Genius Innovations – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Entrepreneurial Spirit</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> My Genius Innovations</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Comprehend detailed technical instructions. Reading: Evaluate texts for bias.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Can comprehend detailed instructions on launching a business, identifying key steps in planning (e.g., "The guide recommends conducting market research before launching a product.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can evaluate bias and perspectives in articles about marketing strategies and use this information to respond to classmates' questions during a debate on how Panamanian entrepreneurs should promote their business ideas (e.g., "One article has emphasized influencer marketing as a key strategy but has ignored its cost and limited reach in local markets. I think small businesses should also consider community-based strategies that build trust.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can summarize steps in technical instructions, preparing an outline for classmates (e.g., "First, brainstorm and create a solid business idea that meets a market need. Next, draft a detailed business plan outlining goals, target audience, and financial projections. Afterward, register the business with the corresponding government entities. Finally, secure financing from banks or investors.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of local Panamanian businesses (e.g., a coffee shop, a handmade craft store, an innovative app startup) and asks students to brainstorm in pairs what steps these entrepreneurs might have taken to launch their ideas. Students share 2-3 ideas with the class. The teacher records key vocabulary on the board (e.g., innovation, business, strategy, launch, promote, costs, target).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models reading a short statement about a business step, emphasizing clear pronunciation, particularly the /ɔː/ sound in words like "launch," "cost," and "talk." For example: "To <b>launch</b> a successful business, one must consider the initial <b>cost</b>." The teacher also models the full vowel in "renewable" /rɪˈnuː.ə.bəl/ and reduced vowel in "successful" /səkˈses.fəl/.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If someone has a 'genius innovation,' what does that mean?" (Expected: A very clever or original new idea/product.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is an 'entrepreneur' responsible for?" (Expected: Starting and running a business, often taking financial risks.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Entrepreneurial Spirit".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students will read an article titled "5 Strategic Steps to Launch Your Business in Panama: A Guide for Young Entrepreneurs." The article provides technical instructions, discusses marketing strategies, and may present a particular perspective on business growth. It incorporates the target grammar (First conditional, Present perfect for innovations, Future continuous) and vocabulary (innovation, business, strategy, marketing, customer base, launch, costs, promote, etc.). The register is informative and professional.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading and interpreting detailed instructions and arguments in an article to understand the process of launching a business and to identify different perspectives or potential biases.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read the article quickly to identify its main purpose. (e.g., "What is the article mainly about? A) The history of Panamanian businesses. B) A step-by-step guide for starting a business. C) Challenges for established companies.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Statements:</b> Students read specific statements and determine if they are true or false based on the text. For example: "The article states that market research should be conducted after launching the product." "Panamanian entrepreneurs have begun using technology to enhance customer engagement."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match each of the "5 Strategic Steps" from the article with its corresponding brief description provided in a separate list.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice identifying and understanding key vocabulary and grammatical structures (First conditional, Present perfect for innovations, Future continuous) within the context of detailed technical instructions and marketing strategies presented in the article. They will also practice reading for specific information to summarize steps.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Cloze):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with sentences extracted from the article, but with key vocabulary words (e.g., 'innovation', 'marketing', 'strategy', 'promote', 'customer base') and grammatical structures (e.g., conditional verbs, present perfect verbs) removed. Students re-read relevant sections of the article to fill in the blanks. Example: "If we ______ (advertise) on social media, we ______ (might reach) a larger customer base." "Many small businesses ______ (begin) using social media to ______ (promote) their products."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled (Sentence Completion):</b> Students complete sentences based on information in the text, focusing on the first conditional and future continuous. For example: "If an entrepreneur wants to reduce costs, they..." (students find the relevant information in the article). "According to the article, before launching the product, I'll be analyzing..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction (Peer Check & Summarization):</b> In pairs, students formulate 3-4 questions about the detailed steps or strategies mentioned in the article, using target vocabulary and grammar (e.g., "What strategies have increased customer engagement?" or "If we establish an online presence, what will be the potential benefits?"). They then exchange questions with another pair and answer them by referring back to the text, clarifying any misunderstandings and checking each other's comprehension.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Entrepreneurial Spirit".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion and Outline Preparation for a Debate.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group will re-read a specific section of the main article (or a supplementary short article on a different marketing strategy) and discuss its instructions and perspectives. Their task is twofold:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Summarize Key Steps:</b> They must extract and summarize the detailed technical instructions provided, preparing a concise outline of the steps an entrepreneur should take (e.g., "First, brainstorm and create a solid business idea...", "Next, draft a detailed business plan...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Evaluate for Bias:</b> They must critically evaluate the text for any potential bias or specific perspectives presented (e.g., "This article has heavily emphasized digital marketing, but it has ignored the costs and limited reach in local Panamanian markets. We think small businesses should also consider community-based strategies that build trust.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Each group prepares an outline of their summary and evaluation. They should incorporate the target vocabulary and grammar (first conditional for potential outcomes, present perfect for what businesses have done, future continuous for planning). They will use professional language and show respect for each other's suggestions. For example, "Your idea adds an interesting approach to our evaluation of this strategy." This outline will be used in the next lesson's debate.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy (observation checklist, rubric, or peer assessment).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group work and a quick peer-assessment of outlines. The teacher circulates, noting students' ability to comprehend instructions, identify bias, and use target language.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Groups briefly present their prepared outlines (1-2 minutes per group), summarizing the key steps from their assigned text and explaining their identified bias/perspective. They must be ready to answer a quick question from the teacher or another group about their findings.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Comprehension:</b> Accuracy in summarizing technical instructions and identifying key steps.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Critical Thinking:</b> Ability to identify and articulate bias or specific perspectives in the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Language Use:</b> Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., innovation, strategy, marketing, promote, costs) and grammatical structures (First conditional, Present perfect for innovations, Future continuous).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Active participation and constructive contribution within the group.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most important instruction or step you learned about launching a business from today's reading?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What made it challenging (or easy) to identify bias in the text, and why?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did I identify the key steps for launching a business and understand their sequence?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new insights did I gain about evaluating information for bias when reading about business strategies?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did students successfully comprehend the detailed technical instructions and identify instances of bias in the reading materials? What specific vocabulary or grammar points need further reinforcement in relation to reading comprehension?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Were the strategies for identifying bias clear enough? What adjustments or additional scaffolding might be needed for students to more confidently evaluate different perspectives in texts?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "In our next lesson (Lesson 3), we will transition from reading about these business strategies to actively *speaking* and *interacting*. You will use the outlines and evaluations you prepared today to participate in a class debate on how Panamanian entrepreneurs should best promote their innovative business ideas, asking and sharing your insights collaboratively."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>